  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ELINA- Enhanced Livelihoods and Nutrition Adaptation Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ELINA project will build on results and lessons learnt from the implementation of MANA project- ZWE 1116. &#xa0;it&#xa0;will reach target households using the CareGroup approach which&#xa0;strongly uses the LANN+ concepts of Linking Agriculture Natural Resource Management towards Nutrition Security.&#xa0;To increase coverage, and sustain gains of ZWE 1116 MANA project, the project will be implemented in additional wards of Tsholotsho and Nyanga districts and new wards in Umzingwane district.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The direct target group comprises 9,500 households (4,000 households in 7 wards in Nyanga, 4,000 in 7 wards in Tsholotsho, and 1,500 in 4 wards in Umzingwane), based on an average of 2 persons per household participating in measures, this amounts to 19,000 persons. The exact number of persons will be determined in the course of the project participants&apos; registration and recording in the database.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project contributes transitively to the transformation of local food systems in order to achieve sustainable food security through diversification and improvement of diets and strengthening of environmental awareness of 9500 vulnerable households in the districts of Umzingwane, Tsholotsho and Nyanga in Zimbabwe.9,500 vulnerable households in 18 communities/wards of Umzingwane, Tsholotsho and Nyanga districts have improved their dietary diversity and livelihoods through improved agricultural and livestock production, sustainable natural resource management, improved access to safe water, community-based enterprises, seed banks, and the use of appropriate nutrition practices.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="DE-1" role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Germany - Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development</narrative>
  </participating-org>
